    "title": "UWPR Safety",
    "excerpt":"UWPR and EH&amp;S Resources   UWPR safety guidelines   All UWPR users must read and abide by the Safety Guidelines.      No food in the lab.   Always wear appropriate clothing and Personal Protective Equipment.  Gloves, goggles and disposable lab coats are available for you to use.  If you can’t find them or are unsure what PPE to use, come ask us to help you.   Do not use any of the equipment unless you were trained by UWPR personnel.   Review the SOP’s before using any chemicals.   Make sure your EH&amp;S training is up to date, including the “Compressed Gas Safety” training to use the pressure cells. You can check the status of your training records here:  EH&amp;S My Training   University of Washington Laboratory Safety Manual   UW Laboratory Safety Manual  Laboratory Specific Infromation (pdf)  Laboratory Specific Emergency Infromation (pdf)   Personal Protective Equipment (PPE)   UW EH&amp;S PPE page  UWPR PPE assessment (docx)   University of Washington MSDS/SDS Search   new UW MSDS/SDS Search UW net ID required  MyChem UW net ID required   UW Chemical Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs)   UW EH&amp;S SOP’s  Contact EH&amp;S 206-616-3778   UWPR SOPs      Acetic Acid (Organic Acids) (pdf)   Acetonitrile (pdf)   AMMONIUM CARBONATE (Irritant) (pdf)   Buspirone hydrocholide (Accute toxins) (pdf)   Butylamine (pdf)   Caffeine (Accute toxins) (pdf)   CESIUM IODIDE (Irritant) (pdf)   CALCIUM CHLORIDE DIHYDRATE (Irritant) (pdf)   DITHIOTHREITOL (DTT) (Accute toxins) (pdf)   Ethanol (Flammable solvents) (pdf)   Formamide (pdf)   Fluoranthene (pdf)   Formic Acid (Organic Acids) (pdf)   FLEXMIX MS STANDARDS (Accute toxins) (pdf)   Gas Cylinder (pdf)   HydrochloricAcid (pdf)   Iodoacetamide (Accute toxins) (pdf)   IODOACETIC ACID (Irrinant_2) (pdf)   Isopropanol (Flammable solvents) (pdf)   LAEMMLI SAMPLE BUFFER (Irrinant_2) (pdf)   LITHISIL 829 POTASSIUM LITHIUM SILICATE SOLUTION (Irritant) (pdf)   Methanol (Flammable solvents) (pdf)   PBS PHOSPHATE BUFFERED SALINE (Irrinant_2) (pdf)   PIERCE CALIBRATOR SOLUTION (Accute toxins) (pdf)   POTASSIUM SILICATE SOLUTION (Irritant) (pdf)   Reserpine (pdf)   SDS (pdf)   SILICA GEL (Irritant) (pdf)   Trifluoroacetic Acid (Organic Acids) (pdf)   TRIPLE QUAD CALIBRATION SOLUTION (Accute toxins) (pdf)   Trypsin (pdf)   TYROSINE (Irrinant_2) (pdf)   ULTRAMARK(R) 1621 (Irrinant_2) (pdf)   UWPR floor plan, Assembly area, building fire safety evacuation plan (FSEP)   B59 Mass spec lab floor plan (pdf)  Download B59 Mass spec lab floor plan (pptx)  SLU_Arial_Campus_Evac_Staging_Locations for building D (pdf)  2023 FSEP Building D (Updated 2.13.23).pdf  all SLU fire safety evacuation plan (FSEP), are located here (UWP Net ID required)   University of Washington Accident Prevention Plan   UW Accident Prevention Plan  The University’s Accident Prevention Plan covers the anticipated occupational hazards that generally apply to employees across the University. It outlines policies and procedures implemented to reduce or eliminate these hazards.   Genome Sciences Supplemental Accident Prevention Plan   Laboratory Risk Assessment Tool (Lab R.A.T.)   Laboratory Risk Assessment Tool (Lab R.A.T.)  Tool for researchers to systematically identify and control hazards to reduce risk of injuries and incidents.  UWPR LabRAT assessments are in a folder located on the shelf next to the flammable cabinet in Brotman B59   Online Accident Reporting System (OARS)   OARS Reporting an Incident online  Report any work-related injury or illness to your supervisor as soon as possible. Then report it to the Environmental Health and Safety Department (EH&amp;S) via the UW Online Accident Reporting System (OARS). Submit the OARS report within 24 hours.   EH&amp;S Health and Safety Resources   Please note these links to important health and safety resources:           Chemical Safety Overview  Chemical SOP Templates  Hazardous Chemical Waste Disposal  MyChem            Research and Lab Safety Overview,  Safety Manuals  Emergency Washing Equipment  Compressed Gas and Cryogenic Fluids,  Sharps Safety            Safety Training,  Lab Safety Training Matrix,            Workplace Safety Overview  Accident and Injury Reporting,  Personal Protective Equipment (PPE)       The new Report a Concern form allows you to anonymously report any safety concern or potentially hazardous situation before an accident or injury occurs.   Please visit the EH&amp;S website and familiarize yourself with the new layout and helpful tools.   Visit the Lab Safety Dashboard for Safety inspection and Self-Inspection Report PI log-in URL website and familiarize yourself with the new layout and helpful tools.     Quick Links      COVID-19 Prevention   UWPR Safety guidelines   Lab Safety Manual   PPE   UW MSDS/SDS search   Standard Operating Procedures   UWPR Floorplan   UW accident prevention plan   Lab R.A.T.   OARS   EH&amp;S Resources  ","url": "https://proteomicsresource.washington.edu/methods/safety/"
